      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="6" column="0" colspan="2">
      <widget class="QCheckBox" name="flagUse1Point71FormIDSpace">
       <property name="whatsThis">
        <string>&lt;p&gt;Skyrim Special Edition version 1.6.1130 fixed an internal loading bug, making it possible for game data files to use form IDs in the range [xx000000, xx0007FF] as long as they have at least one master. This update also incremented the internal version number for game files from v1.70 to v1.71.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The update isn't exclusive to ESL files, but it affects them the most, by doubling the number of forms they can contain. However, v1.71 data files can cause older versions of Skyrim Special Edition to crash, unless they install the Backported Extended ESL Support mod.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
       </property>
       <property name="text">
        <string>Use extended ESL form ID space</string>
       </property>
       <property name="checked">
        <bool>true</bool>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item row="7" column="0" colspan="2">
      <widget class="QCheckBox" name="deleteEmptySeq">
       <property name="text">
        <string>Delete SEQ file if empty</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
